Statements in Java:
Types of statements in java:
 - Expression Statement
 - Declaration Statement
 - Control Statements

 1. Expression Statement
    int temp ++;
 2. Declaration Statement
    int x=10;//declaration statement
    boolean b=true;
 3. Control Statement
   - Selection Statement (if,else,if-else)
   - Jump Statement / Switch Statement
   - Iteration Statement (loops)
     for : When the number of iterations is known in advance.
         : Entry-controlled (checked before executing the body).
       Minimum Iteration: 0

     for -each : When sequentially traversing arrays or collections.
               : Automatic (continues until the end of the collection).
       Minimum Iteration: 0 (if collection is empty)

     while
         : When the number of iterations is unknown beforehand.
         : Entry-controlled (checked before executing the body)
          Minimum Iteration: 0

     do-while
          : When the code must execute at least once regardless of the condition.
          : Exit-controlled (checked after executing the body).
          Minimum I.iteration: 1

     Jump Statement:
          : break
          : continue
